INSERT INTO categories (name, tagline, sort_order, mod) VALUES ('Nelua · Stranger systems building blocks', 'Ambitious proposals with small, inspectable first experiments.', 6, 'nelua') ON CONFLICT (name) DO UPDATE SET tagline = excluded.tagline, sort_order = excluded.sort_order, mod = excluded.mod;
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-borrow', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Safer systems contracts', 'Scoped borrowing and escape checks', 'Catch references that outlive their storage.', 'Reject a returned stack reference or a reference-capturing closure stored past its frame. Start with bounded checks rather than full lifetime inference.', 'Extend analysis of local references, borrowed spans and by-reference captures; validate with compiler examples and Nelibc buffers.', 'Aliases through raw pointers, imported C and calls need explicit boundaries; bounded checking is not a memory safety proof.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 1, 0, 'low', 'large', 0, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-capabilities', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Safer systems contracts', 'Function capability contracts', 'State which functions may allocate, block or call platform services.', 'An allocator helper or signal handler reports the exact call that introduces a forbidden dependency.', 'Check explicit contracts transitively across known callees; require declared contracts at foreign and indirect-call boundaries.', 'Separate allocation, blocking and platform effects precisely; unknown callbacks must not silently count as safe.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 1, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-typestate', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Safer systems contracts', 'Resource typestate', 'Make legal resource transitions visible in types.', 'An open handle can be read; a closed handle cannot. Starting a device queue consumes its configured state.', 'Prototype owned wrappers with distinct state types before deciding whether compiler support is needed.', 'Error recovery and partially completed transitions must preserve ownership without excessive wrapper code.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'high', 'medium', 2, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-storage', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Safer systems contracts', 'Caller-supplied storage', 'Use bounded output and scratch buffers consistently.', 'A formatter or parser accepts your storage and reports required capacity or useful partial progress.', 'Design library conventions for spans, scratch regions, allocator choice and failure semantics; try Nelibc formatting wrappers.', 'Partial writes and required-size reporting need precise contracts. Existing spans do not establish storage lifetime.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'high', 'medium', 3, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-named-variants', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Data, errors and representation', 'Named variant cases', 'Distinguish alternatives even when their payload types match.', 'Read(fd) and Write(fd) are separate cases with the same descriptor representation.', 'Extend variant construction and exhaustive match to named cases; prove it on protocol messages and parser nodes.', 'Define namespacing, zero initialization and compatibility with existing type-based variants.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 1, 0, 'medium', 'large', 4, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-distinct', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Data, errors and representation', 'Distinct types and controlled conversions', 'Keep descriptors, byte counts, pages and addresses apart.', 'Adding a byte count to an address is permitted; adding two file descriptors is rejected.', 'Prototype distinct wrappers and selected operators, then assess a representation-preserving type declaration.', 'Define explicit conversion, ABI, generic matching and which operations preserve the distinct type.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 1, 0, 'medium', 'medium', 5, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-arithmetic', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Data, errors and representation', 'Explicit checked arithmetic', 'Choose checked, wrapping or saturating operations deliberately.', 'Compute allocation count times element size and handle overflow before reserving memory.', 'Provide consistent integer operations and checked narrowing; align compile-time evaluation with generated C.', 'Signed overflow, target widths and conversion edges must have defined semantics in both evaluators.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 1, 0, 'high', 'medium', 6, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-errors', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Data, errors and representation', 'Typed errors and propagation', 'Preserve failure information with Result(T, E).', 'A parser distinguishes invalid input, truncated input and insufficient output capacity, with exhaustive handling.', 'Start with a variant-backed library and explore propagation that composes with existing optional question-mark syntax.', 'Success and error payloads may have the same type; propagation and owned payload cleanup need clear rules.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'medium', 7, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-binary-layout', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Data, errors and representation', 'Binary layout descriptions', 'Describe byte order, field widths and validation together.', 'Parse ELF or TZif data and packets without treating wire bytes as native structs.', 'Generate bounded readers and writers from a compile-time schema; verify offsets independently of native C layout.', 'Unaligned access, malformed lengths, overflow and versioned formats require explicit behavior.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'high', 'medium', 8, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-platform-config', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Platforms and hardware', 'Validated compile-time platform descriptions', 'Build and validate static platform configuration in one place.', 'A platform without a clock explicitly rejects timed waits or selects an unsupported-operation implementation.', 'Extend typed compile-time configuration into callback validation, operation tables and generated bindings; try Nelibc host operations.', 'Distinguish an absent capability from a runtime failure. Keep the core independent of workshop consumers.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'high', 'medium', 9, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-mmio', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Platforms and hardware', 'Typed hardware memory access', 'Give device registers access rules beyond ordinary memory.', 'A write-only register cannot be read, and a write-one-to-clear register gets an appropriate operation.', 'Prototype register accessors with widths and permissions; add compiler support only where emission guarantees require it.', 'Volatile access is not an atomic or ordering guarantee. Architecture-specific barriers and exact access widths need validation.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 10, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-relative-refs', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Platforms and hardware', 'Relative references into regions', 'Store checked offsets instead of process-specific pointers.', 'Move or map a data structure at a new base and resolve its references against an explicit region.', 'Prototype region-bound offsets and checked resolution for shared memory or mapped data.', 'Region identity, alignment, overflow, mutation and temporary pointer lifetime all need contracts.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 11, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-state-machines', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Language experiments and tools', 'Typed protocol and state-machine descriptions', 'Describe states, messages and legal transitions together.', 'A protocol handler handles every legal input and makes forbidden transitions explicit.', 'Use syntax extensions and compile-time generation of ordinary records and dispatch; start with a small incremental protocol.', 'Define failure transitions, ownership and async boundaries; avoid claiming that a generated machine verifies the whole protocol.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 12, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-generators', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Language experiments and tools', 'Generators with visible storage', 'Suspend and resume a function through a caller-owned state record.', 'An incremental parser resumes as bytes arrive without a separate stack or implicit heap allocation.', 'Lower suspension points into explicit state and lifecycle operations with a documented layout policy.', 'Ownership, references across suspension, cleanup and cancellation are major design questions.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'low', 'large', 13, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-typed-holes', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Language experiments and tools', 'Typed holes for development', 'Ask the compiler what belongs in an unfinished expression.', 'A placeholder reports the expected type, available bindings and unmet generic constraints.', 'Add a diagnostic-only placeholder that cannot enter an executable; try it in generic and compile-time examples.', 'Keep suggestions bounded and accurate in the presence of forward inference and unresolved types.', 'Nelua systems, Nelibc, firmware and driver developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'high', 'medium', 14, 1, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-content-addressing', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Code with an identity', 'Content-addressed definitions', 'Give code a stable identity beyond its file and spelling.', 'Rename or move a helper without changing its identity; inspect exactly which implementation and dependencies a program uses.', 'Prototype an optional index of canonical, resolved typed definitions and dependency hashes. Keep text files as the editing format and C as an output. Derive artifact-cache keys separately from code identity, target, toolchain and build inputs. Inspiration: Unison content-addressed definitions.', 'Hash equality is not behavioral equivalence. Recursive groups, nominal type identity, macros and mutable globals need explicit rules. Foreign implementation versions and exported ABI names must be accounted for; a source hash does not pin a host libc.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'low', 'large', 15, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-dependency-patches', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Code with an identity', 'Dependency-aware upgrade plans', 'Treat an upgrade as an explicit change to a code graph.', 'Preview every caller affected by replacing one parser definition, retain the old version, and inspect failed type checks before applying the upgrade.', 'Use stable definition identities to map old dependencies to replacements; recheck affected users and let the developer accept a reviewable patch. Start with a Nelibc helper upgrade.', 'Matching types does not prove matching behavior. Preserve tests and ABI checks; coexistence of native versions needs symbol isolation, and patches must not silently change global state.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 16, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-structural-refactors', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Code with an identity', 'Structural code queries and refactoring', 'Search and transform resolved code rather than matching spelling.', 'Find every call to a particular imported operation even when it has aliases, then preview a typed replacement across the project.', 'Expose a read-only typed-code query API first, then transactional rewrite plans with source locations, hygiene and type checking. A content-addressed index can supply stable references.', 'Generated syntax, macro provenance and formatting complicate rewriting. Identity alone does not prove a rewrite correct; always expose the resulting source diff.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 17, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-compute-capsules', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Code with an identity', 'Portable computation capsules', 'Package an explicitly portable function and its inputs for another machine.', 'Send a pure packet-analysis task to a build server; it resolves the exact code dependencies and returns a typed result.', 'Define a restricted portable subset with canonical value encoding, a dependency manifest and an explicit remote executor. Compile or locate a native artifact for the destination target rather than sending raw process memory.', 'Ordinary pointers, file handles and C imports cannot travel implicitly. Code identity grants no authority or sandbox: admission, execution limits, authentication and target compatibility are separate requirements.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'low', 'large', 18, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-effect-handlers', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Effects, time and changing programs', 'Algebraic effects and handlers', 'Write a clock or storage request once; choose its implementation around the call.', 'Run the same state machine against a real clock, a simulated clock or a deterministic test log.', 'Explore typed effect requests and lexical handlers as a separate proposal from capability restrictions. Begin with non-resuming or single-resumption handlers that lower to explicit context records and calls. Inspiration: Unison abilities.', 'Resuming a continuation interacts with stack references, ownership and cleanup. Multiple resumption needs a separate design; imports and callbacks cannot claim undeclared effects are absent.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'low', 'large', 19, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-record-replay', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Effects, time and changing programs', 'Deterministic record and replay', 'Turn a hard-to-reproduce systems failure into a replayable input trace.', 'Capture clock, randomness and platform-operation results, then rerun a protocol state machine from the same starting state.', 'Record at declared effect or platform boundaries; version trace schemas and code identities. Start with a single-threaded Nelibc host consumer before addressing scheduling.', 'Raw C, MMIO and unrecorded I/O break determinism. Replay must suppress external writes; concurrent scheduling and sensitive trace data require explicit policies.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 20, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-durable-functions', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Effects, time and changing programs', 'Durable functions that survive restarts', 'Persist progress at deliberate suspension boundaries.', 'A firmware update coordinator resumes after a power loss without repeating an already acknowledged step.', 'Lower an opt-in function into a versioned state machine with serializable locals, explicit durable storage and logged effect receipts. Build on visible generator storage rather than serializing a native stack.', 'Exactly-once external effects require cooperation or reconciliation, not just a saved continuation. Upgrades need migrations; pointers and live locks cannot be persisted as ordinary locals.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'low', 'large', 21, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-live-patching', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Effects, time and changing programs', 'Live patching with state migration', 'Replace a running component at a declared safe point.', 'Change a long-running host tool or simulator while preserving state through an explicit migration function.', 'Start in hosted user-space with versioned dispatch tables, quiescence points, layout checks and opt-in state migrations. Keep static freestanding builds on their existing path.', 'Active frames, borrowed references, TLS and old callbacks can retain the prior implementation. Define rollback and reclamation; matching hashes or ABI layouts alone do not make a patch safe.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'low', 'large', 22, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-incremental-computation', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Effects, time and changing programs', 'Incremental computations', 'Recompute only the pure derived values affected by an input change.', 'Adjust one device configuration field and refresh the dependent tables and diagnostics while retaining unrelated work.', 'Prototype a library of explicit input cells and pure dependency-tracked computations with invalidation and bounded caches. Explore compiler assistance only after a concrete consumer.', 'Hidden mutation and effects invalidate cached results. Cycles, cache lifetimes and deterministic dependency discovery need rules; this does not make arbitrary Nelua code reactive.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 23, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-specialization', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Stranger systems building blocks', 'Partial evaluation and specialization', 'Fix part of a program input and generate a smaller specialized function.', 'Specialize a packet decoder for a known schema while leaving packet bytes as runtime input.', 'Explore an opt-in specialization operation over typed code, with explicit static arguments and code-size budgets; emit ordinary Nelua IR and C. This goes beyond folding a call whose result is entirely known.', 'Prevent specialization explosions and preserve overflow, aliasing and evaluation-order semantics. Foreign calls and effects limit what may be evaluated early.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 24, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-refinements', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Stranger systems building blocks', 'Bounded refinement constraints', 'Carry simple facts such as ranges and alignment with a value.', 'A validated packet length can be passed to a bounded decoder without losing the fact that it fits the buffer.', 'Start with integer ranges, alignment and constant relationships at function boundaries. Discharge a small decidable subset statically and require explicit validation for the rest.', 'A length fact does not establish pointer validity or lifetime. Mutation can invalidate relationships; define runtime-check behavior and avoid pretending a general theorem prover is available.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'low', 'large', 25, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-session-endpoints', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Stranger systems building blocks', 'Session-typed communication endpoints', 'Check both sides of a message exchange against their protocol.', 'A worker must receive configuration before sending a result, and consuming an endpoint advances its permitted operations.', 'Represent protocol states and dual endpoints using owned types first; generate typed send and receive operations over an explicit transport. Prototype an in-process worker exchange.', 'Message loss, cancellation, branching and protocol upgrades need explicit outcomes. Static sequencing alone does not guarantee deadlock freedom or reliable delivery.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 26, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-address-spaces', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Stranger systems building blocks', 'Typed address spaces', 'Keep CPU, device, DMA and remote addresses distinct.', 'A device-visible DMA address cannot accidentally be dereferenced as a CPU pointer; mapping it requires the platform capability.', 'Prototype distinct address-space parameters and explicit map/unmap APIs around existing pointers. Later assess backend support for targets with separate memory spaces.', 'An address-space tag does not perform cache synchronization, grant access or establish lifetime. IOMMU mappings, ownership and target-specific representations remain explicit contracts.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 27, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-region-snapshots', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Stranger systems building blocks', 'Transactional region snapshots', 'Checkpoint an owned data region and reopen a consistent version.', 'A simulator or embedded state store commits a new graph of records and recovers the previous valid snapshot after an interrupted write.', 'Combine region-relative references, versioned schemas and copy-on-write or journaled updates. Begin with a user-space file-backed library and fault-injection tests.', 'Crash consistency depends on actual storage ordering and flush guarantees. External effects cannot be rolled back with memory; concurrent writers and migrations need defined protocols.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 28, 2, 0)
INSERT INTO ideas (id, mod, category, title, pitch, experience, how, risks, audience, in_world, tos_safe, top_pick, wow, feasibility, effort, sort_order, added_version, retired) VALUES ('nelua-logic-rules', 'nelua', 'Nelua · Stranger systems building blocks', 'Declarative logic rules', 'Describe derived facts and let a bounded rule engine find the consequences.', 'Derive which platform operations or device dependencies are reachable, and show the chain of facts behind an answer.', 'Prototype a syntax-extension library for typed facts and monotone rules compiled into explicit worklists and indexed tables; use it on a small platform configuration.', 'Require finite domains or resource bounds. Negation, deletion and incremental updates need defined semantics; rule evaluation may allocate unless storage is explicitly supplied.', 'Nelua compiler, Nelibc, firmware and systems-tool developers', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'medium', 'large', 29, 2, 0)
